<div>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-[10px] pb-[40px]">
        <h3 class="text-display-32 font-semibold">Key Findings of SOFI 2026</h3>
        <p class="font-light">The 2026 State of Food Security and Nutrition in the World (SOFI 2026) presents a cautiously optimistic picture of global food security. For the third consecutive year, global hunger declined, reflecting gradual recovery from the disruptions caused by the COVID-19 pandemic, economic downturns, and the global food price crisis. Yet the report cautions that current progress remains far too slow to achieve Sustainable Development Goal (SDG) 2: Zero Hunger by 2030. More importantly, SOFI 2026 argues that the global food security agenda must move beyond increasing food production toward ensuring that everyone has access to healthy, affordable, and sustainable diets (FAO et al. 2026).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-[10px] pb-[20px]">
        <h4 class="text-display-24 font-semibold">Southeast Asia at a Glance: Food Security and Nutrition</h4>
        <p class="font-light">Key Regional Highlights</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-[20px] pb-[20px]">
        <div class="rounded-xl p-[30px] bg-[#008C67] w-[300px] text-white">
            <p class="text-display-42">14%</p>
            <p class="font-light">of Southeast Asia's population continues to experience food insecurity, despite sustained economic growth and improvements in agricultural productivity (FAO 2025).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl p-[30px] border-[1px] border-[#D3D3D3] w-[300px]">
            <p class="text-display-42">228M</p>
            <p class="font-light">people across ASEAN, roughly one in every three residents, cannot afford a healthy diet, highlighting that food affordability has become one of the region's most pressing food security challenges (FAO 2025).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl p-[30px] bg-[#008C67] w-[300px] text-white">
            <p class="text-display-42">6.4%</p>
            <p class="font-light">The Asia-Pacific region reduced the prevalence of undernourishment to this figure in 2024, equivalent to approximately 25 million fewer hungry people than the previous year (FAO et al. 2025).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl p-[30px] border-[1px] border-[#D3D3D3] w-[300px]">
            <p class="text-display-42">~40%</p>
            <p class="font-light">The region still accounts for nearly this share of the world's undernourished population, indicating that progress remains uneven (FAO et al. 2025).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl p-[30px] bg-[#008C67] w-[300px] text-white">
            <p class="text-display-42">3×</p>
            <p class="font-light">Southeast Asia continues to experience the triple burden of malnutrition, where child stunting and micronutrient deficiencies coexist with rapidly increasing rates of overweight, obesity, and diet-related noncommunicable diseases (FAO et al. 2025; UNICEF, WHO, and World Bank 2025).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl p-[30px] border-[1px] border-[#D3D3D3] w-[300px]">
            <p class="text-display-42">2026–30</p>
            <p class="font-light">ASEAN has responded by prioritizing food and nutrition security, climate resilience, digital transformation, and sustainable agriculture under the ASEAN Food, Agriculture and Forestry Sectoral Plan (FAF-SP) 2026–2030 (ASEAN 2025).</p>
        </div>
        <p class="font-light">Climate change is becoming a major driver of food insecurity in the region. More frequent floods, droughts, typhoons, sea-level rise, and saltwater intrusion are threatening agricultural productivity, fisheries, and rural livelihoods, particularly among smallholder farmers (ADB 2023).</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-[20px]">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-[20px]">
            <h4 class="text-display-24 font-semibold">Global hunger continues to decline but remains alarmingly high</h4>
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-[20px]">
                <p class="font-light">SOFI 2026 estimates that 645 million people, or 7.8% of the world's population, experienced chronic hunger in 2025. This represents a decline from 8.1% in 2024 and 8.6% in 2022, equivalent to approximately 43 million fewer hungry people over the past three years (FAO et al. 2026).</p>
                <p class="font-light">Asia continued to drive much of the global improvement. According to the Asia and the Pacific Regional Overview of Food Security and Nutrition 2025, approximately 25 million people in Asia and the Pacific escaped hunger in 2024, reducing the regional prevalence of undernourishment to 6.4%, down from 7.0% in 2023. Despite this progress, the region still accounts for nearly 40% of the world's hungry population, with almost 80% of those affected living in Southern Asia (FAO et al. 2025).</p>
                <p class="font-light">Within Southeast Asia, progress has likewise been encouraging but uneven. While several ASEAN Member States have substantially reduced hunger through economic growth, agricultural modernization, and expanded social protection programs, food insecurity remains persistent among vulnerable populations, particularly in rural and climate-exposed communities.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-[20px]">
            <h4 class="text-display-24 font-semibold">Food insecurity extends beyond hunger</h4>
            <div>
                <p class="font-light">SOFI distinguishes hunger from broader food insecurity. Approximately 2.1 billion people continue to experience moderate or severe food insecurity, meaning they lack regular access to sufficient, safe, and nutritious food (FAO et al. 2026).</p>
                <p class="font-light">Although Asia has one of the lowest regional prevalence rates of moderate or severe food insecurity (20.3%), the absolute number of affected people remains substantial because of the region's large population (FAO et al. 2026).</p>
                <p class="font-light">For Southeast Asia, food insecurity is increasingly associated with income inequality, climate-related disasters, and disruptions in food supply chains rather than insufficient food production alone. During the 47th ASEAN Ministers on Agriculture and Forestry (AMAF) Meeting, ASEAN acknowledged that approximately 14% of Southeast Asia's population continues to experience food insecurity, emphasizing the need for stronger regional action to ensure equitable access to nutritious food (FAO 2025).</p>
            </div>
        </div>


        <div class="flex flex-col gap-[20px]">
            <h4 class="text-display-24 font-semibold">The affordability of healthy diets remains the greatest challenge</h4>
            <div>
                <p class="font-light">Perhaps the report's most important finding is that 2.69 billion people 32.7% of the global population cannot afford a healthy diet, despite improvements in food production and economic recovery. In 2025, the average global cost of a healthy diet increased to PPP $4.28 per person per day, reflecting persistent structural inefficiencies across agrifood value chains (FAO et al. 2026).</p>
            </div>
        </div>
       <div class="pb-[40px]">
            <div class="font-light flex flex-col gap-[24px] py-[30px] px-[20px] rounded-xl border-[1px] border-[#D3D3D3] mb-[20px]">
                <div>
                    <div class="flex justify-between text-[14px] mb-[8px]">
                        <span>Global population that cannot afford a healthy diet</span>
                        <span class="font-medium">32.7%</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="w-full h-[6px] bg-[#E5E3DA] rounded-full overflow-hidden">
                        <div class="h-full bg-[#B59637] rounded-full" style="width: 32.7%"></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="flex justify-between text-[14px] mb-[8px]">
                        <span>ASEAN population that cannot afford a healthy diet</span>
                        <span class="font-medium">~33%</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="w-full h-[6px] bg-[#E5E3DA] rounded-full overflow-hidden">
                        <div class="h-full bg-[#B59637] rounded-full" style="width: 33%"></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="flex justify-between text-[14px] mb-[8px]">
                        <span>Southeast Asia experiencing food insecurity</span>
                        <span class="font-medium">14%</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="w-full h-[6px] bg-[#E5E3DA] rounded-full overflow-hidden">
                        <div class="h-full bg-[#B59637] rounded-full" style="width: 14%"></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div class="flex justify-between text-[14px] mb-[8px]">
                        <span>Asia-Pacific share of world's undernourished</span>
                        <span class="font-medium">~40%</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="w-full h-[6px] bg-[#E5E3DA] rounded-full overflow-hidden">
                        <div class="h-full bg-[#B59637] rounded-full" style="width: 40%"></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <p class="font-light">The challenge is equally significant in Southeast Asia. According to FAO, approximately 228 million people in ASEAN roughly one in every three residents cannot afford a healthy diet (FAO 2025). The affordability gap is driven not only by household income constraints but also by high post-harvest losses, weak cold chain infrastructure, fragmented food supply chains, and limited access to diverse and nutritious foods. These findings reinforce SOFI's central argument that improving food security requires transforming agrifood systems rather than simply increasing staple crop production.</p>
        </div>

        
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-[20px] pb-[40px]">
            <h4 class="text-display-24 font-semibold">The triple burden of malnutrition persists</h4>
            <div>
                <p class="font-light">SOFI 2026 highlights the growing coexistence of undernutrition, micronutrient deficiencies, overweight, and obesity. While child stunting has continued to decline gradually, progress remains insufficient to meet the 2030 global nutrition targets. At the same time, obesity and diet-related noncommunicable diseases continue to increase across all regions (FAO et al. 2026).</p>
            </div>
            <div class="flex gap-[40px]">
                <div class="border-[1px] border-[#D3D3D3] rounded-xl p-[40px] flex flex-col items-center gap-[20px] w-[30%]">
